# Domain modules

A domain's **source location is declared, not assumed**: `config/domains.php` is the registry, and `DomainManager` resolves every path (`domainPath`, `providerPath`, `apiRoutePath`, `testsPath`) through it. A domain either lives under `app/Domain/{Domain}/` or, when its entry carries `package`, inside a Composer path package under `packages/{slug}/`.

## Path packages (core domains)

- **Why:** a downstream project must be able to consume a core domain without forking this repo. A path package keeps the code in place while Composer installs it as a real dependency (`silverspoonmedia/platform`, `silverspoonmedia/navigation`, `silverspoonmedia/notification`, `silverspoonmedia/audit`, `silverspoonmedia/billing`, `silverspoonmedia/ai`).
- **The kernel is the platform package.** `silverspoonmedia/platform` ships `App\Support\*`, `App\Domain\Identity\*`, `App\Http\{Controllers,Requests,Resources,Middleware}`, `App\Repositories\*`, `App\Providers\{Encryption,Product,DomainAccess,Settings,Domain\Identity}*`, `App\Rules\*`, `App\Traits\*`, `App\Exceptions\*`, and its `autoload.files` loads `src/Support/Settings/helpers.php` (root `composer.json` must **not** load it again — double declaration is fatal). Every non-kernel package declares `"silverspoonmedia/platform": "^1.0"`. Code the packages import is edited in `packages/platform/src/`, not `app/Support/`; the host keeps only its four product-coupled overrides (`app/Support/Product/Services/{ProductAnalyticsService,ProductInsightService}.php`, `app/Support/ListActions/Builders/{HashBlocklistQueryRowActions,MicrostockCredentialQueryRowActions}.php`), `AppServiceProvider`, the product providers, and the domain console commands. Kernel migrations stay host-owned (`users`, `permission_tables`, `system_settings`, `product_*`, `identity_oauth_accounts`): the package ships models for a host-owned schema.
- **One package may carry more than two core domains.** A package is a distribution unit, not a taxonomy mirror: domains consumed together ship together. `silverspoonmedia/audit` = ActivityLog + ErrorLog, `silverspoonmedia/billing` = PaymentGateway + Currency + Service → one PSR-4 prefix, registry entry and API route file **per domain**, one `composer.json`, one provider, one `tests/` tree. Bundling never merges namespaces.
- **Namespace never changes.** A packaged domain keeps `App\Domain\{Domain}\*` mapping to `packages/{slug}/src/`. Callers do not learn a vendor namespace, and translation keys do not move.
- **Host overrides win.** Root `composer.json` declares `"App\\Domain\\Navigation\\": "app/Domain/Navigation/"` explicitly so Laravel's own autoloader entry precedes the package entry in the generated PSR-4 map. Dropping that line makes `app/Domain/Navigation/...` dead code that silently loses to the package. One prefix per domain in a bundle. The same rule keeps the kernel overrides alive: root re-declares `App\Support\`, `App\Http\`, `App\Repositories\` and `App\Domain\Identity\` over `app/`.
- **Package contents:** `src/`, `routes/{domain}.php` — one per domain, no prefix or name, the host applies those (a single-domain package may use `routes/api.php`) — `config/`, `database/{migrations,seeders,factories}/`, `resources/lang/{locale}/**`, `tests/`. The provider is auto-discovered via `extra.laravel.providers`; it calls `mergeConfigFrom`, `loadMigrationsFrom`, `translator->getLoader()->addPath(...)`, binds contracts, and registers listeners/commands explicitly. Never re-register any of that in `bootstrap/*`.
- **Package tests run in place, not in isolation.** Each package has a `Package:{slug}` suite in `phpunit.xml`, so its `tests/` runs alone; the full run covers them anyway, since PHPUnit runs every suite in the file. A directory may sit in exactly one suite — twice makes PHPUnit warn per file and exit non-zero on a green run. Those tests still extend `Tests\TestCase`, use `Tests\Concerns\*` and boot the whole monolith: a standalone run needs Orchestra Testbench plus a fixture stubbing the kernel contracts, and no package has one. `tests/Domain/Core/PackageTestSuiteTest.php` fails on a package that ships tests nobody wired, or a directory wired twice.
- **Registry entry:** `'package' => 'silverspoonmedia/{slug}'`, `'path' => 'packages/{slug}/src'`, `'routes' => 'packages/{slug}/routes/{domain}.php'`, optional `'provider'`, optional `'web'` for a server-side web route. Bundled domains share `package`/`path`/`provider` and keep their own `routes`. `kind`/`locked`/`parent` are unaffected. **Registry order is route load order** — a domain whose file was split out of a sibling keeps the URI position it had before (Currency before Service in `silverspoonmedia/billing`), so never alphabetize the entries.
- **Config ownership is per file, not per package:** a published vendor config the host owns stays in the host (`config/activitylog.php`, Spatie's, carries `sensitive_properties.*`), while the domain's own config moves (`packages/audit/config/errorlog.php`).
- **Routes** load through `DomainManager::packageApiRoutePaths()` in `routes/api/v1.php` and `DomainManager::packageWebRoutePaths()` in `routes/web.php` (a packaged domain's `web` key, applied inside the `web` group); `config/*.php` stays in the package, so deleting it from the host is correct, not a regression (`setting_config('notifications.delivery')` is Tier B and unaffected).
- **Dependency direction:** a core package may import `App\Support\*` and `App\Domain\Identity\Models\{User,Role,Permission}`; the kernel imports a package only through a kernel-owned contract (`App\Support\Navigation\PresentedTreeEpoch`, `App\Support\Encryption\DecryptionAuditRecorder`, `App\Support\ErrorLogging\ExceptionRecorder`, `App\Support\ActivityLog\{SubjectAliasRegistrar,SubjectLabelRegistrar}`, `App\Support\Billing\{FulfillmentRegistry,FulfillmentContext}`, `App\Support\Notifications\Contracts\NotificationDispatcher`, `App\Support\Broadcasting\Contracts\ChannelRegistrar`, `App\Support\Encryption\Contracts\LegacyColumnMigrator`, `App\Support\Ai\AiUsageConsolidatorRegistry` + `App\Support\Ai\Contracts\{AiUsageLedger,AiUsageConsolidator}`), never a package interface, and only behind `app()->bound(...)` so a host without the package still boots. A core package never imports a product domain, and never another core package: a seam to a sibling is a kernel contract the *owning* package implements — `NavigationServiceProvider` registers `menu` on the audit package's `SubjectAliasRegistrar` and a `MenuSubjectLabelPresenter` on `SubjectLabelRegistrar`, and a product registers its `FulfillmentHandler` on the kernel `FulfillmentRegistry` that `silverspoonmedia/billing` consumes, or its ledger on the `AiUsageLedger` binding and `AiUsageConsolidatorRegistry` that `silverspoonmedia/ai` consumes. `tests/Domain/Core/DependencyDirectionTest.php` enforces all three halves — `KERNEL_KNOWN_EXCEPTIONS` is empty, and a non-kernel package that skips the `silverspoonmedia/platform` require fails too; adding a package import to a sibling, the kernel, or the package→product direction fails it.
- **Version pinning:** path repositories infer the version from the current git branch, so each package declares `"version"` explicitly and the host requires `"*"`. Without it `composer update` fails against `minimum-stability: stable` on any non-main branch.
- **Distribution is one-way.** `packages/{slug}/` in this repo is the source; `github.com/silverspoonmedia/{slug}` is a read-only mirror produced by `scripts/publish-packages.ps1` (`git subtree split` + tag). Never commit to a mirror, and never delete `version` from the monolith copy — it is dropped only in the tagged mirror commit. Contract: [core-packages.md](../../docs/integration/core-packages.md#distribution).
- Windows: `"symlink": true` produces a junction and works; if it ever fails, set `"symlink": false` and run `composer update silverspoonmedia/*` after every change under `packages/`.
- Packaged domains are still **platform core**: `domain:remove` refuses them, and their code leaves by editing the package, not by scaffolding.

## Registry axes (all domains)

- Three axes, never collapsed into one label: `kind` (`core` = foundation, `product` = sold surface), products only `locked` (whether `domain:remove` refuses), and the composition axis `parent` below. Core is additionally pinned by `DomainManager::PLATFORM_CORE` — flipping `kind` in config cannot make a core domain removable.
- **Composition axis `parent` (product only):** a **subproduct** declares the product domain it extends (`'parent' => 'Archivd'`; Microstock is the only one). It is a full product — own key, activation, RBAC, SKU, namespace, `uninstall.json` — **never** a third `kind` value. `DomainManager::parentOf()` / `childrenOf()` expose it; `domain:list` prints the `Parent` column; `domain:make --parent={Product}` registers one (the parent must already be a registered product); `domain:remove` refuses a parent while a registered child points at it, so a subproduct never outlives its base.
- **Never** run `domain:remove` on a core domain, or on a product while `locked => true`. Unlock is a deliberate `config/domains.php` edit; there is no `domain:unlock`.
- `domain:make` always scaffolds a **product** (locked by default) with `Http/{Controllers,Requests,Resources}`, `Services`, `Repositories`, `Models`, tests, `{Name}RoleSeeder`, and a starter `uninstall.json`; it never touches migrations. `domain:remove` deletes PHP/routes/tests/provider only — migrations stay unless `--purge-data` asks for them.
- **Product domains carry an uninstall manifest**: `app/Domain/{Name}/uninstall.json`, schema `domain-uninstall/v1`. It is the reviewed map of everything the domain touches — `delete` paths across backend/SPA/docs, `edits` (shared-file surgery from a closed op vocabulary), `data` (tables, migrations, RBAC, rows), and `ignore` (survivor references, each with a reason). It lives inside the domain because it dies with the domain.
- **Every file a product domain touches outside `app/Domain/{Name}/` is recorded in that domain's `uninstall.json` in the same task** — route/config/lang/SPA/docs file, `DatabaseSeeder` line, env key, `docs-coverage.json` entry. `DomainUninstallManifestTest` fails on an unlisted reference, so the manifest cannot drift. A `.gitignore`d machine-local override is not repo content: it is not scanned and not recorded, and the hand edit it still needs goes in `notes`.
- `domain:remove {Name}` reads the manifest: bare run prints the plan then confirms; `--dry-run` prints plan + unlisted references and changes nothing (allowed while locked); `--draft-manifest` writes a scanner draft and removes nothing; `--force` skips the prompt without skipping the `unresolved` check; `--purge-data` additionally drops the recorded tables/rows/RBAC and deletes the recorded migrations, and is refused unless `DestructiveDatabaseCommandGuard` allows it (`ALLOW_DESTRUCTIVE_DB=true` outside sqlite/local). No `uninstall.json` → the structural behaviour plus an explicit warning.
- Sibling checkouts resolve as `dirname(base_path()).'/monolith-vue-workers'` and `'/docs'`; an absent sibling is reported **unverifiable** (never as clean) and its manifest section is skipped, never silently passed.
- Removal procedure for the AI that runs it: [.cursor/skills/domain-remove/SKILL.md](../../.cursor/skills/domain-remove/SKILL.md) — schema and op vocabulary stay in [docs/platform/reference-architecture.md](../../docs/platform/reference-architecture.md#domain-uninstall-manifest), the single owner.
- Namespaces: `App\Domain\{Domain}\Models|Services|Http\{Controllers,Requests,Resources}`. Shared infra stays `App\Support\*`, `App\Http\Middleware\*`, `App\Repositories\Eloquent\EloquentCrudRepository`.
- **Do not** import one domain's services into another. `App\Domain\Identity\Models\{User,Role,Permission}` is the sanctioned hub; anything else is explicit and documented.
- **Do not** conflate the module registry with the other axes that reuse `core`/`product`: RBAC `domain_kind` on Spatie roles/permissions (Identity only), per-user product activation (`product_activations` + `product.active`), per-domain visibility (`product_domain_visibilities` + `domain.access:{Domain}`), and `product_analytics` counters. Each has its own owner and its own gate.
- Product H-RBAC: add roles/permissions with `domain_kind = product` and globally unique names (`Billing Admin`, never a second `Admin`). Never overload or rename core roles.
- New product routes: gate with `domain.access:{Name}` **before** `product.active:{Name}` / `permission:`.
- Loader order is presentation only — core requires first, product last, in `routes/api/v1.php`, `bootstrap/providers.php`, and `config/domains.php`. It never changes URL paths or route names.
- Details: [docs/platform/architecture.md](../../docs/platform/architecture.md), [docs/platform/reference-architecture.md](../../docs/platform/reference-architecture.md).
